    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d87-a1">

                <pb facs="0180" n="100" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg100"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron de Favereau to Mr. Townsend.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-12-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi> 2,
                            1902</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: In your letter of November 19 your
                    excellency was kind enough to inform me that you had been requested to have
                    transmitted to the King, my august sovereign, the sincere congratulations of the
                    President and people of the United States by reason of his having happily
                    escaped from harm.</p>
                <p>His Majesty was much touched by this kind message, and he has requested me to
                    have recourse to the obliging medium of your excellency in order to transmit to
                    their respective objects the expression of his sincere thanks.</p>
                <p>Please accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">De Favereau.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
